{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118076","id":3477746415,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7PSjLv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118076","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118076.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118076.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118076","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118076/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118076/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118076/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f9145cbc7262994ef9aabdff3929244b244f0a83","number":118076,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Apple, Wayland] HDR Output: Emit window events when HDR state changes","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**This is a followup PR to #115666.** The original PR's commit has been included in this PR.\r\n\r\n### What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Parent PR #115666 adds events for Windows, but does not add events for Apple and Wayland. This PR adds these events.\r\n- Similar to the parent PR: scripts must poll `Window.get_output_max_linear_value()` ever frame, which is inefficient because it normally does not change until the user changes their screen brightness, for example.\r\n- #118079 needs these changes to show HDR info of the game window without polling constantly.\r\n\r\n### What is the rationale for the approach used in this PR?\r\n\r\nJust like #115666, this allows scripts on all platforms to change scripts that used to be:\r\n\r\n``` GDScript\r\nfunc _process(_delta: float) -> void:\r\n\tvar output_max_linear_value = get_window().get_output_max_linear_value()\r\n\t# Do something with output_max_linear_value\r\n```\r\n\r\nInto something more efficient like this:\r\n\r\n``` GDScript\r\nfunc _enter_tree() -> void:\r\n\tvar window: Window = get_window()\r\n\twindow.output_max_linear_value_changed.connect(_on_output_max_linear_value_changed)\r\n\t_on_output_max_linear_value_changed(window.get_output_max_linear_value())\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _exit_tree() -> void:\r\n\tget_window().output_max_linear_value_changed.disconnect(_on_output_max_linear_value_changed)\r\n\r\n\r\nfunc _on_output_max_linear_value_changed(output_max_linear_value: float) -> void:\r\n\t# Do something with output_max_linear_value\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Was generative AI (LLM AI) used to create a portion of this PR?\r\n\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n### Are there any parts of this PR that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers?\r\n\r\n- It may be more convenient to test this PR with #118079 because this followup PR makes use of the signal introduced by this PR.\r\n- For Apple, I renamed `void DisplayServerMacOSEmbedded::send_window_event(...)` to  `virtual void DisplayServerMacOSEmbedded::send_window_event_by_id(...)` and moved it to the base class to allow `DisplayServerMacOS` to use it as well. As a part of this, I changed `DisplayServerMacOS::send_window_event(...)` to be `const`, but I could instead change `virtual void send_window_event_by_id(...)` to be non-`const` if that's preferable.\r\n- Let me know if I should squash the original PR and add a co-author if that's preferable to merging the two PRs separately, one after the other.\r\n\r\nI've tested this to find it works well on iOS, macOS, and Fedora KDE plasma.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097519,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1MTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:ios","name":"platform:ios","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097780,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc3ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:macos","name":"platform:macos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url"